Z||000000||86SEFIERO||02-04-2001||03:23 PM||||<BR>What has to be done to the engine cradle in the 88 cars to make the v-8 swap work? Can this be done by yourself instead of paying 300 dollars to have it done if im on a tight budget. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||02-04-2001||07:21 PM||||Archie's website <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  has instructions for doing the mods. You should be able to figure out from those how much welding oyu have to do. If not, call Archie. I hear he is always willing to help.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||02-05-2001||12:51 AM||||The Zumwalt/Corson/HTD/Fiero Conversion Plus & all the other Zumwalt copies, do require some heavy modifications to the 88 Fiero engine cradle. All of those modifications are  needed because the Zumwalt (& copies Et al) Move the engine over to the left in the car some 2"+. However on my kit we don't move the engine over to the left like that and the only modifications to the '88 cradle (& all other cradles) are the drilling of 2 holes.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SEFIERO||02-05-2001||02:31 AM||||Thanks for the reply Archie!!1 When I do my v-8 swap it's definitly going to be with your kit.||||reg||1
